{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A psalm. Ascribe to YHWH, O sons of Elim</b> — הבו — perhaps the vowel of the he changes on account of a guttural letter, like את אשר תאפו אפו." "<b>And sons of Elim</b> — they are the stars, and the proof: ברן יחד כוכבי בקר, and after it: ויריעו כל בני אלהים, and the meaning is doubled. The reason for mentioning the stars is that according to their arrangement the rains descend with the help of the Elohim of gods, and he mentioned הבו לה' another time, for so it always is, in the manner of: נשאו נהרות ה'." "<b>The meaning of ascribe to YHWH</b> — is ascribing, in the manner of תנו עוז, that they acknowledge that might and glory belong to HaShem alone." "<b>The meaning of and bow down</b> — like the bowing of a servant to his master, when he is willing to do what he commands him. And the meaning: for the stars have no ability to change their movement or the ways of their arrangement."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "Reading הזכיר for what appears to be הזכיר in the source; standard sense preserved."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:59.938333536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}